        "PMC9962455::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting CoCrFeNiTi alloy is a simple, single-phase solid solution.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9962455::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting or as-cast CoCrFeNiTi alloy has minimal or no detectable short-range order.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Equimolar CoCrFeNiTi has relatively low hardness and strength.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Equimolar CoCrFeNiTi has favorable plasticity and machinability.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Limited short-range order governs the combination of low hardness and strength with favorable plasticity in equimolar CoCrFeNiTi.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8357793::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Limited short-range order lowers resistance to dislocation motion and lattice friction.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8357793::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Limited short-range order facilitates double-kink nucleation in screw dislocations.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8357793::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Limited short-range order enhances edge-dislocation mobility.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lower lattice friction and easier dislocation motion reduce hardness and yield strength.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lower resistance to dislocation motion improves ductility.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Controlled annealing can induce varying degrees of short-range order in equimolar CoCrFeNiTi.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The thermal treatments are intended to leave the overall alloy composition unchanged.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Increasing short-range order impedes dislocation mobility.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8357793::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Induced short-range order will increase hardness and yield or compressive strength relative to the as-cast state.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
